# Meerkat TaskPanel host configuration — generated by `install.sh`.
#
# The host-external supervisor reads this file. It is installed as a host-local copy —
# `<host>/meerkat-taskpanel/scripts/supervisor.mjs` — not run from the checkout, so
# nothing here has to name the checkout for the loop to be *loadable*. It holds two
# things:
#
#   MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_CLAIM_UNASSIGNED=yes  also claim unassigned cards (the public pool)
#   MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_CLAIM_UNASSIGNED=no   claim only cards assigned to this agent
#
#   MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_REPO=<path>           where the board engine (`taskctl`) lives
#
#   MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_WORKFLOW=yes|no       run the workflow sub-pass (reconcile,
#                                           review dispatch, applying verdicts)
#   MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_AUTO_ACCEPT_REVIEWS=yes|no
#                                           let the loop close a review card after
#                                           applying its verdict; `no` leaves it for
#                                           a human to accept
#   MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_REVIEWER=<agent>      the independent reviewer; empty means
#                                           deliveries wait for a human
#
# A command-line flag (--claim-unassigned) or the environment variable override the
# claim policy; the file is the installer's remembered answer to
# "Allow claiming unassigned tasks?". The three workflow keys are the installer's
# remembered answers to the same questions; an empty reviewer is a complete answer.
#
# The repo path is recorded because the loop is split: the executor is copied into the
# host, but the board it drives stayed in the checkout. Recording it here is what keeps
# the *scheduling unit* free of checkout paths — a unit a user has already loaded keeps
# working when the checkout moves, and re-running `install.sh` re-points it at the new
# location without a `launchctl` / `systemctl` / `crontab` reload.
MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_CLAIM_UNASSIGNED={{CLAIM_UNASSIGNED}}
MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_REPO={{REPO}}
MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_WORKFLOW={{WORKFLOW}}
MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_AUTO_ACCEPT_REVIEWS={{AUTO_ACCEPT_REVIEWS}}
MEERKAT_TASKPANEL_REVIEWER={{REVIEWER}}
